            <ArticleTitle>Some pain, some gain: reflections on the past two decades of neonatal pain research and treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review reflects back on the progress that has been made in infant pain research over the past 20 years and how the research has influenced (or has failed to influence) the attitudes and practices of health professionals about infant pain. Progress in understanding of infant pain neurobiology, treatment, and measurement are discussed, and new directions for future research are proposed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
